Fix panic "attempt to subtract with overflow" at src/reader/reader.rs:2546.

The forward branch of Reader::jump computes `el.len() - 1` on a usize, so a
repeat-jump (vi `;` / `,`) with Till precision on an empty command line
underflows and aborts the shell. The backward branch already guards with
`tmp_pos > 0`; mirror that by moving the `+ 1` to the left-hand side.

Upstream: not yet fixed as of 4.9.3.

--- a/src/reader/reader.rs
+++ b/src/reader/reader.rs
@@ -2543,7 +2543,7 @@
             }
             JumpDirection::Forward => {
                 let mut tmp_pos = el.position() + 1;
-                if precision == JumpPrecision::Till && skip_till && tmp_pos < el.len() - 1 {
+                if precision == JumpPrecision::Till && skip_till && tmp_pos + 1 < el.len() {
                     tmp_pos += 1;
                 }
 
